Text recognition (OCR) for Folio
================================

A scanned PDF is pictures of pages: there is no text in it to find, select,
copy or read aloud. With this plugin Folio reads the text in those
pictures (optical character recognition, with Tesseract), and the page then
works like any other: Find, selecting, Copy, Define and Read aloud all use
the recognised text. The page itself looks the same.

Using it
--------
Menu > Text recognition:

  Recognise this page     reads the page you're on (even one that has some
                          text of its own, e.g. text drawn as outlines).
  Recognise all pages     reads every scanned page in the background, so
                          Find can search the whole document; the window's
                          title shows the page it has reached. Choose it
                          again to stop.
  Scanned pages as I read (on to start with) reads each scanned page as you
                          come to it, and the next two.
  Accurate / Fast         which data to use (see below).

Reading aloud waits for a scanned page's text before reading it.

A page takes a few seconds (about twice as long with Accurate). It happens
in the background: Folio and the desktop carry on, and a page you scroll to
is drawn first. Pages with text of their own are left alone, except by
Recognise this page.

What's recognised is kept in <Choices$Write>.Folio.OCR, one file per
document, so it isn't done again when you next open the document. You can
delete that folder at any time.

Accurate and Fast
-----------------
Two sets of Tesseract's English data are included:

  Accurate  (about 5 MB) Tesseract's standard English data, without the
            parts for the old Tesseract 3 engine, which Folio doesn't use.
            On test scans it made about half the mistakes of Fast.
  Fast      (about 4 MB) a smaller network: about twice as quick.

Either folder can be deleted to save space; Folio then uses the other.

Good scans (300 dpi, straight, clean) recognise best. Handwriting, unusual
fonts, columns of numbers and pictures of text in photographs may come out
wrong or not at all. Only English is included for now.

Licences
--------
The language data is Tesseract's (https://github.com/tesseract-ocr), under
the Apache License 2.0: see DataLicence. Tesseract itself is part of
Folio's !RunImage (Apache-2.0, through MuPDF).
